menu "espOS BLE provisioning"

    config ESPOS_PROV
        bool "BLE provisioning (credentials from a phone, no access point)"
        default n
        depends on BT_BLUEDROID_ENABLED
        select ESP_PROTOCOMM_SUPPORT_SECURITY_VERSION_2
        help
            Lets a phone hand this device its WiFi credentials over BLE GATT
            instead of the setup access point.

            Off by default: it costs about 23 KB of flash and only makes sense
            on a device that has BLE at all. It needs Bluedroid; the
            application must already have brought the stack up (espos_ble does
            this, including the ESP32-P4's hosted co-processor path).

            NOTE this is built on protocomm directly, NOT on
            espressif/network_provisioning, because that component's manager
            drives the WiFi station itself and espOS's own state machine
            already owns those calls. The practical consequence is that
            Espressif's "ESP BLE Provisioning" phone app will NOT talk to this
            device -- it speaks the manager's protobuf schema. The endpoint
            here is plain JSON. See docs/provisioning.md.

            While provisioning is active BLE SCANNING IS SUSPENDED: Bluedroid
            keeps a single GAP callback and protocomm takes it, so a gateway
            left scanning would receive nothing at all and report no error.

    config ESPOS_PROV_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Stop advertising after this many seconds (0 = never)"
        default 600
        range 0 86400
        depends on ESPOS_PROV
        help
            A device left advertising for provisioning is a device anyone in
            range can try to configure. The default gives ten minutes to get
            a phone out, then closes the window.

endmenu
